sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-16> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The skeleton of the nassellarian Callimitra reproduces the interfacial film system of four soap-bubbles in tetrahedral contact (six plane interfaces meeting in threes at 120°, edges meeting near 109°), so it must have been formed at the interfaces of a tetrahedral group of cells.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Callimitra's skeleton is formed on the interfaces of a tetrahedral group of four cells";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "six plane interfaces meeting in threes at 120^\\circ; edges meeting at \\approx 109^\\circ 28'";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter IX, “On Concretions, Spicules, and Spicular Skeletons”; topic “Nassellarian tetrahedral skeletons”. Scope: Nassellaria with tetrahedral skeletons (e.g. Callimitra)"
}
